#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Trafalgar: Nelson's last battle, 21 October 1805.  A sample game for
the Grognard engine, and its first at sea.

Off Cape Trafalgar the Combined Fleet of France and Spain, 33 ships of
the line under Villeneuve, straggles north in a ragged crescent, back
towards Cádiz.  Down on it from the west, before a light wind, come 27
British ships in two columns: Nelson's in the Victory, Collingwood's in
the Royal Sovereign, to break the line in two places and fight it out
ship against ship.  Play either side against the computer, or against a
friend at the same screen.

Run it with ./trafalgar (Python 3 with Tk, nothing else).  The game is
saved to ~/.trafalgar.json.  ./trafalgar --selftest checks the map and
plays a game between two computer players.
"""

